                'category' => 'Prepositions and Conjunctions',
                'theory' => "Complex prepositions (также называемые phrasal prepositions) — устойчивые словосочетания из нескольких слов, которые вместе функционируют как один предлог.\n\nКогда используется:\n— место/положение: in front of, in the middle of, next to, on top of: The car is in front of the house.\n— причина: because of, due to, owing to: The match was cancelled because of the rain.\n— противопоставление/уступка: in spite of, despite: In spite of the traffic, we arrived on time.\n— добавление/соответствие: in addition to, according to, on behalf of: According to the forecast, it will rain tomorrow.\n\nФормы:\nin front of, in spite of, because of, due to, instead of, on behalf of, in addition to, according to, in the middle of, on top of, out of.\n\nПримеры:\nThe bus stop is in front of the school. Due to bad weather, the flight was delayed. I'll speak on behalf of the whole team. In addition to English, she speaks French and German. According to the news, prices will rise.\n\nДополнительные примеры:\nWe went for a walk in spite of the cold. Instead of taking the bus, we walked. The cat was sitting on top of the fridge. Because of the noise, I couldn't sleep. He acted out of pure kindness.\n\nЧастые ошибки:\n— because вместо because of перед существительным: 'because the rain' — неправильно, нужно 'because of the rain'.\n— despite of (лишний of): 'despite of the rain' — неправильно, нужно либо 'despite the rain', либо 'in spite of the rain' (despite само по себе уже не требует of).",
